<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grover Cleveland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1837">1837</a>–<a href="/years/1908">1908</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grover Cleveland was the 22nd and 24th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, serving from 1885 to 1889 and from 1893 to 1897. A Democrat who opposed high tariffs and defended the gold standard, he withdrew the treaty to annex <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> in 1893 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blount-report">Blount Report</a> found American complicity in the queen's overthrow. His second term was dominated by the economic depression that followed the Panic of 1893.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grover-cleveland.jpg" alt="Grover Cleveland" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Napoleon Sarony · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StephenGroverCleveland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Michigan&quot; and &quot;The Song of Iowa&quot;, of the &quot;Ode to Labrador&quot;, of college songs in the United States and China, of the Boy Scouts' &quot;Scout Vespers&quot;, of a Swedish schoolchildren's song about the bus driver, and of &quot;Democrats, Good Democrats&quot;, a campaign song for <b>Grover Cleveland</b> in 1884.</blockquote><a href="/songs/o-tannenbaum">O Tannenbaum</a></li><li><blockquote>President <b>Grover Cleveland</b> dedicated Liberty Enlightening the World, a gift from the people of France, on Bedloe's Island.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-28">28 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>President <b>Grover Cleveland</b> withdrew the treaty and, after the Blount Report found American complicity, asked for the queen's restoration.</blockquote><a href="/state/provisional-government-of-hawaii">Provisional Government of Hawaii</a></li><li><blockquote>When President <b>Grover Cleveland</b> refused to annex Hawaii, the Provisional Government of Hawaii called a constitutional convention.</blockquote><a href="/state/republic-of-hawaii">Republic of Hawaii</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Princeton, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.35,-74.66&amp;year=1883" aria-label="Princeton on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2716 721 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Grover Cleveland"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3166 991h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3166 991h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=40.35,-74.66&amp;year=1883">What was here in 1883? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="enc-words" id="in-their-words"><h2 class="enc-section-title">In their words</h2><blockquote class="enc-q"><p>&#8220;…the lesson should be constantly enforced that, though the people support the government, the government should not support the people.&#8221;</p><footer>Veto of the Texas seed bill, 16 February 1887 &#183; original &#183; <a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Cleveland%27s_Veto_of_the_Texas_Seed_Bill" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a></footer></blockquote><blockquote class="enc-q"><p>&#8220;Federal aid in such cases encourages the expectation of paternal care on the part of the government and weakens the sturdiness of our national character…&#8221;</p><footer>Veto of the Texas seed bill, 16 February 1887 &#183; original &#183; <a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Cleveland%27s_Veto_of_the_Texas_Seed_Bill" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a></footer></blockquote><blockquote class="enc-q"><p>&#8220;Every citizen owes to the country a vigilant watch and close scrutiny of its public servants and a fair and reasonable estimate of their fidelity and usefulness.&#8221;</p><footer>First Inaugural Address (1885) &#183; original &#183; <a href="https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/925/pg925-images.html" rel="noopener">Project Gutenberg</a></footer></blockquote><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/encyclopedia/quotations">Quotations from 535 people &rarr;</a></p></section>
